\"/tier-list?rank=epic\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankTierListLink\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Epic\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Epic\",\"name\":\"Ruby\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"49.35\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Ruby\",\"delta\":\"-0.18%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.20\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.50\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Epic\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"legend\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-[3px]\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"linear-gradient(to bottom, #4dc9f6, #4dc9f633)\",\"boxShadow\":\"0 0 12px -2px #4dc9f680\"}}],[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-2 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-x-3 gap-y-1 flex-wrap\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline gap-2.5 text-sm md:text-base font-heading font-semibold text-text-primary uppercase tracking-[0.06em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-block rounded-sm px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.16em] self-center\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#4dc9f6\",\"background\":\"#4dc9f61a\",\"border\":\"1px solid #4dc9f640\"},\"children\":\"Legend\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankCardH3\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Ruby\",\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L40\",null,{\"href\":\"/tier-list?rank=legend\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankTierListLink\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Ruby\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"49.76\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Ruby\",\"delta\":\"+0.23%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.28\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.39\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-[3px]\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"linear-gradient(to bottom, #f59e0b, #f59e0b33)\",\"boxShadow\":\"0 0 12px -2px #f59e0b80\"}}],\"$La0\",\"$La1\"]}],\"$La2\",\"$La3\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The simplest draft test is this: if the fight you expect is front-to-back and crowded, Ruby makes sense. If the fight you expect is long-range poke into disengage, she does not.\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The one thing that makes Ruby work\"]}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Ruby is not a flat lifesteal fighter. She is a displacement engine whose sustain scales with danger and whose skills now actually hurt.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Her passive is the whole story. Basic attacks do not trigger her lifesteal pattern, but her skills do, and every skill cast gives her a short dash plus temporary defense that stacks. The 2.1.88 change matters here: she no longer banks big heals while she is healthy, but the lower her HP drops, the harder her lifesteal ramps. That rewards the exact thing she is built for, staying in a fight that is going badly until it turns. If you stand still and try to auto like a standard bruiser, you have turned off the part of the kit that matters.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Be Good! is lane control and, after the buff, real damage. The swing plus shockwave lets Ruby tag a wave and the enemy EXP laner at the same time, and the slow is what sets the next angle. Don't Run, Wolf King! is the actual trade reset. The double swing interrupts movement, tugs people back into your space, and buys time for the passive dash out. I'm Offended! is no longer just engage. It is a heavy, long-cooldown commitment that both straightens a messy front line and deletes a real chunk of whoever it catches, so you spend it on the fight that matters, not the first one you see.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"That is why Ruby feels oppressive in the right game and mediocre in the wrong one. She does not win by walking up and stat-checking. She wins by making the enemy spend movement and spacing twice in the same trade while she slides out, drops low, and heals harder the deeper the fight goes.\"}]\n84:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first five minutes\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Start with S1 and make the first wave do double duty.\"}],\" Hit the melee minions and clip the enemy EXP laner with the same Be Good! cast. Ruby does not need a flashy level 1. She needs the wave moving on her terms and the opponent slowed long enough to think twice about stepping forward for the next last hit.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Take S2 at level 2 and hold it until they cross your line.\"}],\" The mistake is throwing Don't Run, Wolf King! the moment it comes up. Let them walk into the minion wave first, then use the pull and double stun when they have already committed their step. That is the trade Ruby wins most often because the return path is simple: cast, dash sideways, reset.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Save Flicker or Vengeance for the first real skirmish, not for lane vanity.\"}],\" Flicker matters when it converts an ult into a numbers advantage around Turtle. Vengeance matters when the enemy jungler finally joins the lane and tries to burst through your control window. Burning either spell for a tiny solo kill before minute 5 usually turns the next objective fight into a bad one.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Freeze the lane if your jungler is pathing top side. Thin the wave and keep the fight near your turret if the enemy mid is missing. Ruby can survive pressure better than many EXP laners, but she still loses if she spends S2 into fog and the counter-gank arrives before the passive dash is back.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The two-item window that decides her game\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Ruby's first real spike is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"War Axe plus Queen's Wings\"}],\", usually around the 8 to 10 minute mark in a stable EXP game.\"]}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"War Axe gives her exactly what early Ruby wants: HP, cooldown reduction, spell vamp, and a stacking damage passive that rewards staying in contact. Ruby does not burst people in one clean rotation. She keeps touching the fight long enough for the stack count to matter, then forces you to keep fighting while her cooldowns come back. War Axe is the item that makes those repeated half-commits hurt.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Queen's Wings is what turns that pressure into survival with teeth. The spell vamp and cooldown reduction keep the passive dash loop running, and Demonize triggers below 40% HP: 30% damage reduction for three seconds plus two seconds knocked off her cooldowns, exactly when the reworked low-HP lifesteal is ramping hardest. It rewards the same behavior Ruby already rewards, staying low and staying in, so once it lands, matchups that were merely annoying in lane become manageable and the burst window that used to end her after the first control chain starts closing on its own.\"}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-13\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"This is the window where Ruby stops being \\\"hard to kill\\\" and becomes \\\"hard to play into.\\\" Before these two items, she can start fights but cannot always stay in them. After them, she can take first contact, live through the answer, and force a second crowd-control cycle before the enemy carry is comfortable again.\"}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-14\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Dominance Ice is the alternative second item when the enemy draft is built around sustain or shields. Its passives punish anyone who stays near her: Fortress Shield stacks Hybrid Defense for every enemy hero in range, and Lifebane cuts their Shield and HP Regen to 60% of normal, so the anti-sustain idea survives. But as a default it is the wrong second buy: it gives no spell vamp or cooldown reduction, and Ruby's engine needs both. Take Queen's Wings second, then buy Dominance Ice third when the team is not already covering anti-heal.\"}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"$La4\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8e:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning and target priority\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The common Ruby mistake is opening every fight with Flicker-Ult just because the combo exists. That is highlight behavior, not consistent winning behavior, and after the 2.1.88 cooldown change a wasted ult leaves you without your biggest swing for a long stretch of the fight.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Ruby is usually better as the second touch in a fight, not the first. Let the tank or jungler force the first turn of heads, then enter once the enemy backline has taken one step forward or one step sideways. That is when her pull changes from a gimmick into a punish.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Stand one skill-length behind your first engager.\"}],\" Close enough to follow instantly, far enough that you do not eat the same first wave of crowd control. Ruby wants to arrive after the enemy commits, not before.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Pull across your team, not deeper into theirs.\"}],\" If your ult drags people toward a wall, a turret, or the rest of your lineup, it is good. If it drags you past the midpoint with no help behind you, it is self-sabotage. The direction of the pull matters more than the number of targets.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Use the passive dash sideways more often than forward.\"}],\" After S1 or S2, the instinct is to chase with the dash. In real teamfights the better dash is usually diagonal or sideways, because it keeps the enemy carry inside your control radius while moving you out of the cleanest return damage angle.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"If your support is Mathilda, Angela, or Estes, Ruby can take a much greedier first step because there is actual follow-through behind it. If your support is Diggie into anti-engage or your backline is the real win condition, hold Ruby as peel and let the enemy walk into S2 first. She is one of the few EXP laners who can play either job in the same draft.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: locked slots and real flexes\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Ruby's build is not six locked items. It is a skeleton with a few conversations that matter every game.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"$La5\",\" Tough Boots is the default when the enemy has layered magic CC or a Valir style lane that tries to keep you out forever. Warrior Boots are better when the real problem is physical poke and repeated side-lane trading. Magic Boots only make sense when the enemy has low hard CC and you know you can spend the extra cooldown speed aggressively instead of using it to die faster.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La6\",\"\\n\",\"$La7\",\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\"]\n8f:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Ruby\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"90:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6b\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_1232_1/100_af21c0dd8b5308c27974bff900803a9a.png\",\"alt\":\"Phoveus - Chains of Sin\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"priority\":\"$undefined\",\"fetchPriority\":\"$undefined\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300\",\"sizes\":\"56px\",\"placeholder\":\"blur\",\"blurDataURL\":\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj48cmVjdCB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgZmlsbD0iIzBkMTIyNSIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex-1 min-w-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading font-bold text-text-primary group-hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors truncate\",\"children\":\"Phoveus\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\"